# PlayHouse Multi-Repo Workspace Configuration

This workspace root contains shared configuration for the PlayHouse multi-repo workspace.

## Workspace Skills

Skills in `.cursor/skills/` provide cross-repo capabilities:

| Skill | Purpose | Use When |
|-------|---------|----------|
| task-management | Multi-repo task lifecycle with persistent state | Creating, updating, finishing tasks |
| workspace-navigation | Navigate the multi-repo workspace | Finding files, checking workspace state |
| git-branching | Branch management across repos | Creating/switching/merging branches |
| task-planning | Structured implementation planning | Starting features, breaking down work |

## Workspace Rules

Rules in `rules/` are automatically applied:

| Rule | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| multi-repo-workspace.mdc | Guidelines for working across multiple repositories |
| task-context.mdc | Manifest-based task state management |
| preserve-existing-features.mdc | Ensure existing functionality isn't broken |
| playhouse-operating-loop.mdc | Standard operating procedures |

## Commands

Commands in `commands/` provide quick workflows:

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| review.md | Code review with tests and diff analysis |
| merge.md | Merge task branch (run only after explicit user approval to merge) |

**Policy:** The agent does not merge into `main`/`dev` or push those branches without **explicit user approval** in the conversation. **`multi-tenancy/phase-*`** integration branches are **also protected**: no merge into them and no push without **explicit authorization**. During a phase, tasks are **intended** to land on **`multi-tenancy/phase-N`** (not `main`) once the user approves; merging the phase branch to `main` requires approval again when the phase completes. See `rules/task-context.mdc` and skills `task-management` / `git-branching`.

## Templates

Templates in `templates/` for consistent structure:

| Template | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| task-template.yaml | Starting point for new task manifests |

## Task State

- **Active task:** `current-task.yaml`
- **Task archive:** `tasks/`

## Repository Structure

This workspace includes:

```
.cursor/                    # ← This shared config root
playhouse-web/              # React customer-facing app
playhouse-server/           # Django API backend
playhouse-control-plane/    # Admin UI (React) + Go services
playhouse-cicd/             # Docker/deployment configuration
playhouse-docs/             # Documentation
playhouse-integration-driver/  # On-prem Go driver (WebSocket + hardware)
```

Each repo has its own `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/` for repo-specific configuration.
